{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01FKqQrx9Zo76yS81gBqKPDK","type":"tool_result","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Perfect! I now have all three files you requested. Here's my report:\n\n## 1. Complete Differential Test File Example\n\n**File:** `/private/var/folders/dl/cbns6zkx7txc7pt64b6cgzp40000gn/T/go-unix-utils-worktrees/5523/cmd/base32/base32_test.go`\n\nThis is a comprehensive example showing:\n- `testutils.BuildBinary(t, \".\")` to compile the Go binary\n- `exec.LookPath(\"gbase32\")` to find the reference binary\n- A `tests` slice of `testutils.DiffTest` structs defining test cases with:\n  - `Name`: test identifier\n  - `Args`: command-line arguments\n  - `Stdin`: input data\n  - `Env`: environment variables (with `LC_ALL=C`)\n  - `ExitCode`: expected exit code (defaults to 0)\n  - `Normalize`: optional normalization functions (e.g., discarding stderr)\n- `testutils.RunDiffTests(t, goBin, refBin, tests)` to execute all tests\n\nThe file also includes a separate `TestSIGPIPE` function demonstrating how to test signal handling.\n\n## 2. Full Content of pkg/encutil/decode.go\n\nThe decode module provides:\n- **DecoderConfig struct**: contains a `Decode` function and `IgnoreGarbage` boolean flag\n- **stripWhitespace()**: removes spaces, tabs, newlines, and carriage returns from input\n- **stripGarbage()**: removes non-alphabet characters using `isEncodingAlphabet()` which allows A-Za-z0-9+/=-_\n- **Decode()** function: reads all input, strips whitespace unconditionally, conditionally strips garbage if `IgnoreGarbage` is true, then decodes\n\nThe key flow: read → stripWhitespace → (conditionally stripGarbage) → decode → write\n\n## 3. Full Content of pkg/testutils/difftest.go\n\nThe testutils module provides:\n- **DiffTest struct** with fields:\n  - `Name` (string): test identifier\n  - `Args` ([]string): command-line arguments\n  - `Stdin` ([]byte): input (nil means EOF, empty slice means open stdin immediately closed)\n  - `Env` ([]string): environment KEY=VALUE pairs (merged into inherited env, with LC_ALL=C as default)\n  - `WorkDir` (string): working directory (defaults to t.TempDir())\n  - `ExitCode` (int): expected exit code (defaults to 0)\n  - `Normalize` ([]NormalizeFunc): output normalization functions applied in order\n  - `ExpectedFiles` (map[string][]byte): files created by the test that should be verified\n\n- **RunDiffTests()** function signature:\n  ```go\n  func RunDiffTests(t *testing.T, goBinary, refBinary string, tests []DiffTest)\n  ```\n\n- **NormalizeFunc** type: `func([]byte) []byte` - transformations applied to stdout/stderr before comparison\n\n- **TimestampNormalizer**: a built-in NormalizeFunc that replaces common timestamp patterns with `<TIMESTAMP>`\n\nThe framework runs both binaries with identical inputs, applies normalizers to both outputs, and compares stdout, stderr, and exit codes for divergence."}]}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"9ca46135-07ce-4634-a0ce-ceebccbc4e98","uuid":"c5488999-6f9c-4289-ae2a-38540f2987ea","timestamp":"2026-05-23T12:08:53.572Z","tool_use_result":{"status":"completed","prompt":"I need two things:\n\n1. Find a complete example of a differential test file in cmd/ that uses testutils.BuildBinary and testutils.RunDiffTests. Show me the full content of one such test file (e.g., cmd/base64/base64_test.go or cmd/base32/base32_test.go would be ideal since they're closest to basenc).\n\n2. Show me the full content of pkg/encutil/decode.go so I can understand how whitespace stripping and ignore-garbage work.\n\n3. Show me pkg/testutils/diff.go or whatever file defines DiffTest struct and RunDiffTests function, so I can see the exact struct fields and function signature.\n\nSearch breadth: medium","agentId":"ab0a32098e217f999","agentType":"Explore","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Perfect! I now have all three files you requested. Here's my report:\n\n## 1. Complete Differential Test File Example\n\n**File:** `/private/var/